Description: fast, native graphical Git client
 GerGit is a desktop Git client for Linux, written in C# with .NET and
 Avalonia. Every operation runs the system git command, so repositories,
 hooks and configuration behave exactly as on the command line.
 .
 Features:
  - commit graph with search; branches, remotes, tags, stashes, worktrees
    and submodules in a sidebar; repository tabs and workspaces
  - stage and unstage files, hunks or single lines; commit, amend, and
    commit and push in one step, with live hook and test progress
  - inline and side-by-side diff, image diff, blame and file history,
    external diff and merge tools
  - interactive rebase with drag and drop and a three-pane conflict resolver
  - fetch, pull and push dialogs and automatic background fetch
  - GitHub and GitLab (including self-hosted) accounts: clone from a
    project list, pull and merge requests, notifications
  - Quick Launch, light and dark theme following the desktop, zoom
